Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-19-2001||01:40 PM||||my original seats were the suede or 'pigskin' whatever it was called. I cleaned them with "tannery" and it took a day to dry back out, then I brushed it in one direction with a wide brass tire brush. Believe it or not, kept them really looking nice. At a show a quick brushing again kept them looking new.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||06-19-2001||03:19 PM||||I have the suede seats as well... anyway to remove water stains?  The car came with 'em... I didn't put them there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||06-19-2001||04:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>I have the suede seats as well... anyway to remove water stains?  The car came with 'em... I didn't put them there.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mine had stains too originaly. You cant just wet one spot, if you use any cleaner, you have to dampen the whole seat (either top or bottom) for it to dry with no water marks. Takes quite a while to dry, usually till next day.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ferg||06-19-2001||04:39 PM||||Thanks Roger- I'll have to give it a try. <P>Is 'Tannery' available everywhere?||||reg||1
